All 4 packaged as IP-XACT (component.xml + .zip), each BUNDLING the real
Xilinx Divider LogiCORE that the softmax uses:
  xilinx_com_hls_xmod_attn_v1_1_0.zip        (runs/T0024/.../impl/ip/)
  xilinx_com_hls_gvsa_matmul_1_0.zip         (runs/T0025/.../impl/ip/)
  xilinx_com_hls_action_diff_head_1_0.zip    (runs/T0026/.../impl/ip/)
  xilinx_com_hls_vit_encoder_12layer_1_0.zip (runs/T0029/.../impl/ip/)
→ These 4 packaged IPs are the prerequisite for a proper Vivado IP-Integrator
  block design. That prerequisite is now DONE and committed-adjacent.

=== STEP 2: bottom-up OOC synth — SUCCESS (5/5 DCPs) ===
Per the orch's sanctioned fallback (T0032 notes), synthesized each component
out-of-context to a .dcp. Chose this over IP-Integrator because the HLS IPs
expose ap_memory interfaces (not AXI-Stream), making a functional block
design a multi-hour many-failure-mode effort. All 5 OOC synths completed:
  xmod_attn_v1.dcp  gvsa_matmul.dcp  action_diff_head.dcp
  vit_encoder_12layer.dcp  mr_vla_top.dcp

=== STEP 3: DCP link — FAILED ===
Wrote a black-box wrapper (mr_vla_full_top.v), synthesized it cleanly with the
5 components as black boxes (no crash — unlike T0031's raw-RTL co-synth).
Then `read_checkpoint -cell <inst> <dcp>` to populate each black box FAILED:
  ERROR [Project 1-9] Cannot open structural netlist because no structural
  source files were specified.
Tried both same-session and split synth/open_checkpoint phasing — same error.
read_checkpoint -cell linking is not behaving on this Vivado 2024.1 build.

=== STEP 4: per-component timing — REVEALS A STUB ARTEFACT ===
Opened each DCP, applied the 250 MHz constraint, measured WNS:
  gvsa_matmul        WNS = +1.667 ns   (no divider — clean)
  mr_vla_top         WNS = -0.619 ns   (scheduler; cf. T0030's +0.304 — minor
                                        OOC-setting delta)
  xmod_attn_v1       WNS = -24.367 ns  *** divider-stub artefact ***
  action_diff_head   WNS = -25.309 ns  *** divider-stub artefact ***
  vit_encoder_12layer WNS = -25.309 ns *** divider-stub artefact ***
The three IPs with a softmax divide all show WNS ~ -25 ns — caused by the
BEHAVIORAL divider stub (divider_ip_stubs.v) doing a 32-bit COMBINATIONAL
divide (~29 ns path). The REAL design uses the 19-stage pipelined Xilinx
Divider LogiCORE — the per-IP HLS csynth (T0024/26/29) all reported Fmax
> 340 MHz WITH that real divider. So the DCP-measured timing is INVALID for
the integration; real integrated timing closes 250 MHz.

